WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.810
Euron Greyjoy: Circling the Jade Sea is the
dream of every merchant.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:09.330
On the other side is the Golden Empire of
Yi Ti.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:14.419
Even its ruins dwarf every city in Westeros
and its princes are said to live in houses

00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:19.700
of solid gold and feast on meat powdered with
pearls and jade.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.550
Foolish talk!

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:25.650
If it were true, I would have visited long
ago.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:31.350
But a bold merchant will risk two years for
one voyage to fatten his holds with spices,

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:36.530
gems, and silks so that he never wants for
anything again.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:44.610
To be fair, many never do, because my ship,
Silence, finds them on their return.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:49.470
Their merchant dreams look so pitiful poured
on my decks.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:53.260
Not enough for any lifetime but their own.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:57.960
JaqenH'ghar: A young man walks beside a girl
across a flowered field.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.930
Spring has come, and this girl is his life.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:03.530
He prays.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.960
A child climbs a tree to watch the sunset
over the fields.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.590
Summer is ending, and the harvest is life
for his village.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.220
He prays.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.430
A hunter tracks a boar through the woods.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:20.220
Winter is coming, and this boar is life for
his family.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.770
He prays.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:24.330
But to whom do they pray?

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:29.421
The world has as many answers as there are
men to answer, but walk far enough, climb

00:01:29.421 --> 00:01:33.741
high enough, hunt long enough, and a man shall
find only one.

00:01:33.741 --> 00:01:36.670
One god with many faces.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:42.310
In the Far East, He is the Lion of Night,
who fathered the world's first emperor on

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:46.080
the Maiden-Made-of-Light, and whose wrath
nearly ended the world.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:53.840
In the House of Black and White, however,
He is all of them, and none of them.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:59.280
He is the Many-Faced God, and wherever a man
turns, there He is.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:05.079
Men come from every corner of the world to
know Him, to beg His favor, and seek His gift.

00:02:05.079 --> 00:02:10.759
For themselves, if their life has grown too
hard, or for others who are making it so.

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:13.120
It is all the same to the Many-Faced-God.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:20.080
"Valardohaeris," all men must serve Him, beggars
and kings.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.450
"Valarmorghulis," all men must die, good and
evil.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:30.800
Men worship as they will, but at the end of
every road stands the Many-Faced God, waiting.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:36.140
XaroXhoanDaxos:Our city, however, would be
quite a prize for any empire.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:43.569
Qarth straddles two worlds: a greedy and curious
west and a rich and mysterious east.

00:02:43.569 --> 00:02:48.920
The marvels of Yi Ti and Asshai pass through
our markets and share berths with the riches

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:52.290
of the Free Cities and Westeros.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:57.790
Our ports have fulfilled many a trader's dreams,
almost as many as they have broken.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:02.980
Samwell Tarly: The Maesters don't believe
in prophecy, with good reason.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:06.810
The Children of the Forest supposedly could
see into the future, yet were surprised by

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:11.750
the First Men who nearly ended their race
and the Long Night, which nearly ended us

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.750
all.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.410
Even the wisest Maesters, however, have no
answers for the Red Priests who prophesy about

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.900
the return of the Long Night.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:22.340
For thousands of years, they've kept watch
for the return of The Prince Who Was Promised,

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:27.319
who will be born amid salt and smoke to drive
off the darkness once again.

00:03:27.319 --> 00:03:30.459
Prince of what realm and promised by whom
and to whom?

00:03:30.459 --> 00:03:35.209
The prophecy doesn't say, but at the very
least, it confirmed that not even Essos escaped

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:36.790
the Long Night.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:39.870
I imagine the cataclysm must have confused
the East.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:43.480
Unlike Westeros, they wouldn't have known
of the Night King or the White Walkers or

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.530
the war waged by the First Men and the Children
of the Forest.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.330
They would have just seen a terrible winter
descend and linger far too long until spring

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.720
magically returned to the world.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:04:05.410
Yet somehow, maybe from passing merchants,
maybe in their fires, the Red Priests saw

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:08.220
the truth.

